# ==============================================================================
# RENDER.COM ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES - COPY THESE TO RENDER DASHBOARD
# ==============================================================================
#
# DO NOT commit this file with real values to GitHub!
# This is a template showing what variables you need to set in Render.
#
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Angel One API Credentials
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get these from your Angel One SmartAPI portal: https://smartapi.angelbroking.com
# Copy the exact values from your local .env file

ANGEL_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
ANGEL_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
ANGEL_PASSWORD=your_password_here
ANGEL_TOTP_SECRET=your_totp_secret_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO SET THESE IN RENDER:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Go to your Render dashboard: https://dashboard.render.com
# 2. Click on your "paper-trading-system" service
# 3. Click "Environment" in the left sidebar
# 4. Click "Add Environment Variable"
# 5. For EACH variable above, add:
#    - Key: ANGEL_API_KEY (exact name)
#    - Value: (paste your actual value from .env file)
# 6. Click "Save Changes"
#
# Render will automatically restart your service with new variables.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHERE TO FIND YOUR VALUES:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These are already in your local .env file at:
# c:\trading ai\trading ai\trading-ai\trading_system\.env
#
# Open that file and copy the values after the = sign
#
# Example from your .env:
# ANGEL_API_KEY=OVrdNfkx          <- Copy "OVrdNfkx"
# ANGEL_CLIENT_ID=P53093898       <- Copy "P53093898"
# ANGEL_PASSWORD=YourPass123      <- Copy "YourPass123"
# ANGEL_TOTP_SECRET=ABCD1234...   <- Copy "ABCD1234..."
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY NOTES:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ✅ DO:
#   - Keep values secret
#   - Use Render's environment variable feature (encrypted)
#   - Enable 2FA on your Render account
#   - Keep GitHub repo private
#
# ❌ DON'T:
#   - Commit .env with real values to GitHub
#   - Share credentials with anyone
#   - Use the same credentials on multiple platforms
#   - Hardcode credentials in source code
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERIFICATION:
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# After setting variables in Render, check the logs:
# 
# ✅ Success looks like:
#   [INFO] ✅ Connected to Angel One successfully (Client: P53093898)
#   [INFO] NIFTY: ₹23,683.55
#
# ❌ Failure looks like:
#   [ERROR] Missing Angel One credentials in environment variables
#   [ERROR] Authentication failed: Invalid credentials
#
# If you see errors:
#   1. Double-check each value (no extra spaces!)
#   2. Verify names are EXACTLY: ANGEL_API_KEY, ANGEL_CLIENT_ID, etc.
#   3. Copy-paste from .env to avoid typos
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
